# Conventional Commits template.
# Git strips lines starting with '#'; keep the body wrapped at 72 columns.

# <type>(<scope>): <imperative summary, <= 72 chars>
#
# Types: feat | fix | refactor | perf | test | docs | build | ci | chore | revert
# Scopes: backend | frontend | rag | auth | db | fts | chat | search | docs | ci | deps
#
# Why (the problem this commit solves):
#
# How (the approach, and anything a reviewer would otherwise have to guess):
#
# Verification (exact commands run and their result):
#
# Refs: #<issue>
